  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat (2026-11-18), in his own words:\n\n> and voxel simulation s still broken, no visiable stock removal simulation.\n\n\"Still\" means that he saw this before. No open issue names it. The nearest closed issues are #2181 (stock removal calculated before playback) and #1516 (stock cut only at the end of each move). The first agent that works this issue checks if one of them is the same defect. If it is, reopen that issue with this report and close this one as a duplicate.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe simulation runs, but the stock does not change on screen. The user sees no material removed as the tool moves.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe stock shown at each playback position is the stock after all moves up to that position. A cut is visible.\n\n## Not known yet\n\n- The build or version. The maintainer did not name it.\n- The model, the stock type and the operation types.\n- The engine: dexel column engine (default) or the field engine (`CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field`, #1168).\n- If the stock display is empty, frozen at the first frame, or cut but not drawn.\n\n## First steps for the worker\n\n1. Reproduce on the latest `main` with a headless test: build a part and a simple pocket, run the stock simulation to the end, and assert that the removed volume is greater than zero and that the drawn stock mesh differs from the initial stock mesh.\n2. Find where the chain breaks: the toolpath moves, the removal engine, the mesh update, the draw call. Use `graphify query` first.\n3. Check that the fix does not break the carried-stock and rest-material users of the same engine.\n4. Pin the fix with a test that fails without it. Add the case to the `camcraft-sim` or app test set, in the lowest crate that provides it.\n\n## Safety note\n\nA stock simulation that shows no removal hides what the program cuts. This is `effort:high` by the safety floor. If the engine itself gives a wrong stock (not only a draw fault), raise the priority to P1 and say so in a comment.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test shows visible, correct stock removal after a simple operation.\n- The maintainer's view in the GUI shows the removal (screenshots in the PR body, before and after).\n",
